# Playwright rules (sync API only)

- Use pytest-playwright with the **sync** API; UI tests are plain `def`, not `async def`. Test data is created via sync httpx / API adapters, never via clicks.
- One browser per worker, new context per test. `browser_context_args`, `base_url`, `storage_state` (created by API login once per worker under FileLock; only the login tests skip it).
- Artefacts: `--tracing retain-on-failure --screenshot only-on-failure --video off`.
- Page Object: locators in `__init__` (role/label/test-id first, CSS last), one method per user action, web-first assertions (`expect(...)`) inside `expect_*` methods. Component Objects for repeated widgets (`TaskCard`, `KanbanColumn`).
- Tests read as business flows (`board.create_task(...)`, `board.move_task(task, to=Column.IN_PROGRESS)`). No locators, URLs or sleeps in tests.
- If the frontend lacks accessible names/test ids, list them in `testing/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` and use the most stable selector available. Adding `data-testid` to the frontend is allowed only under `testing-modify-prod.mdc`.
- No `sleep`/`wait_for_timeout`. Max `--reruns 1` in CI, always reported.
- The fast PR subset of UI tests is marked `@pytest.mark.critical` (the `smoke` marker belongs to `tests/smoke/`). Browser synthetic checks live in `tests/synthetic/browser/` (marker `synthetic`), run rarely, and follow the synthetic rules in `testing-core.mdc`.
